    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Mia, why do dogs sniff everything?",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "img:Animals/Servier/dog_beagle",
          "label": "Dog"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "👃",
          "label": "Sniff?"
        },
        "mid": "?"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Because a dog's nose is a superpower! Dogs can smell much, much better than people can.",
      "punch": "superpower",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "👃",
        "text": "A nose superpower!",
        "cue": "superpower",
        "sub": "Much better than ours",
        "sub_cue": "better"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "How is it better?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "A dog's nose has many, many more smell cells than yours. And a big part of its brain works on smells.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "You",
          "items": [
            {
              "icon": "👃",
              "text": "Fewer cells",
              "cue": "yours"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "Dog",
          "items": [
            {
              "icon": "🐶",
              "text": "Lots more cells",
              "cue": "more"
            },
            {
              "icon": "🧠",
              "text": "Big smell brain",
              "cue": "brain"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So what are they smelling on walks?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Clues! A sniff can tell a dog who walked by, if it was a friend, and even what they had for lunch.",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "Sniff clues",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🐕",
            "label": "Who walked by",
            "cue": "walked"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🤝",
            "label": "A friend?",
            "cue": "friend"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🍖",
            "label": "Their lunch",
            "cue": "lunch"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "It's like reading the news with their nose!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Exactly! Sniffing is how dogs read the news. People who study dogs think sniffy walks help them feel happy and calm.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Animals/Servier/dog",
        "text": "Sniffing finds clues",
        "cue": "news",
        "sub": "Sniffy walks, happy dog",
        "sub_cue": "happy"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Why do dogs sniff each other when they meet?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "That's a doggy hello! A quick sniff tells them who the other dog is, kind of like reading a name tag.",
      "punch": "hello",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "👋",
        "text": "A doggy hello!",
        "cue": "hello",
        "sub": "Like a name tag",
        "sub_cue": "name"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Here's a neat trick. When a dog breathes out, air leaves through little slits on the sides of its nose, so new smells keep coming in.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "💨",
        "text": "Side slits on the nose",
        "cue": "slits",
        "sub": "New smells keep coming in",
        "sub_cue": "smells"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Super noses, sniffing clues and doggy hellos. Dogs are amazing sniffers!",
